---
title: Asymptotic family
---

<script>
  import Statement from '$lib/components/statement.svelte';
  import * as affAsymptotics from './statements/aff-asymptotics.svx';
  import * as affAsymptoticsRemark from './statements/aff-asymptotics-remark.svx';
  import * as affFddAsymptotics from './statements/aff-fdd-asymptotics.svx';
  import * as meanFieldAsymptotics from './statements/mean-field-asymptotics.svx';
  import * as sdeAsymptotics from './statements/sde-asymptotics.svx';
</script>

<!-- declare asymptotic family -->
Fix family $(\Xe)_{\epsilon>0}$ of affine processes $\Xe$ with associated conditional distributions $(\Prb^\epsilon_\stateVar)_{\stateVar\in\stateSpace}$ such that the differential $\trunc$-characteristics $(\affDrift^{\trunc,\epsilon}, \affDiff^\epsilon, \affJump^\epsilon)$ relate through the following parameterization.
$$
  @tag(characteristic-asymptotics)
  \affDrift^{\trunc,\epsilon}(\stateVar) = \frac1\epsilon \affDrift^{\trunc,1}(\epsilon\stateVar), \quad
  \affDiff^\epsilon(\stateVar) = \frac1\epsilon \affDiff^1(\epsilon\stateVar), \quad
  \affJump^\epsilon(\stateVar, \rmd\markVar) = \frac1\epsilon \affJump^1(\epsilon\stateVar, \rmd\markVar), \quad \stateVar \in \stateSpace
$$
In effect, for each $\stateVar \in \stateSpace$, the family $(\Prb^\epsilon_\stateVar)_{\epsilon>0}$ is induced by a _base distribution_ $\Prb_\stateVar \defeq \Prb^1_\stateVar$ associated with _base affine process_ $\X \defeq \X^1$ and _base differential characteristics_ $(\affDrift^\trunc, \affDiff, \affJump) \defeq (\affDrift^{\trunc,1}, \affDiff^1, \affJump^1)$.
This also implies a similar parameterization for the Lévy-Khintchine maps $\ode^\epsilon$ associated with $(\affDrift^{\trunc,\epsilon}, \affDiff^\epsilon, \affJump^\epsilon)$ in terms of the base map $\ode$ from $(\affDrift^\trunc, \affDiff, \affJump)$.
$$
  @tag(LK-asymptotics)
  \ode^\epsilon(\momentVar, \stateVar) = \frac1\epsilon \ode(\momentVar, \epsilon \stateVar), \quad \momentVar \in \vecSpace, ~ \stateVar \in \stateSpace
$$
Using the notation of [%full](statement:jump-diffusions-real-moments), we see that the set $\odeSpace(\stateVar)$ of finite points of $\ode(\cdot, \stateVar)$ is identical to that $\odeSpacee(\epsilon\stateVar)$ of $\ode^\epsilon(\cdot, \epsilon\stateVar)$.
So long that $\stateSpace$ is a cone&mdash;which is to say that $\stateSpace$ an additive set, closed under non-negative-scalar multiplication&mdash;we have $\stateSpace = \epsilon\stateSpace$, and so the following sets agree.
$$
  \odeSpace = \bigcap_{\stateVar \in \stateSpace} \odeSpace(\stateVar) = \bigcap_{\stateVar \in \stateSpace} \odeSpacee(\epsilon\stateVar) = \bigcap_{\stateVar \in \stateSpace} \odeSpacee(\stateVar) = \odeSpacee
$$

<!-- show parameterization for \aff -->
Note that a parameterization like [](eq:characteristic-asymptotics) or [](eq:LK-asymptotics) may exist irrespective of the affine property on $(\affDrift^\trunc, \affDiff, \affJump)$.
However, affine processes are distinct in the existence (from [%full](statement:keller-ressel-mayerhofer)) of an affine map $\aff^\epsilon: \momentSpacee \rightarrow \bbR$ respective to $\Xee$,
$$
  \aff^\epsilon(t, \momentVar, \stateVar) = \affPart^\epsilon_0(t,\momentVar) + \bprj{\affPart^\epsilon(t,\momentVar)}{\stateVar},
$$
in which $\aff^\epsilon(\cdot, \momentVar, \cdot)$ is the minimal solution of $\system(\ode^\epsilon, \tau, \momentVar)$ (from [%full](statement:keller-ressel-mayerhofer)) for each $(\tau, \momentVar) \in \momentSpacee$,
$$
  \forall~ \stateVar \in \stateSpace, \quad \left\{\begin{array}{ll}
    \displaystyle \dot\aff^\epsilon(t, \momentVar, \stateVar) = \ode^\epsilon\big( \affPart^\epsilon(t, \momentVar), \stateVar \big), & t \in [0,\tau] \\
    \aff^\epsilon(0, \momentVar, \stateVar) = \prj{\momentVar}{\stateVar}
  \end{array}\right.
$$
and is the cumulant generating function of each marginal.
$$
  \Exp_{\Prb^\epsilon_\stateVar} \exp\prj{\momentVar}{\Xee_\tau} = \exp\aff^\epsilon(\tau, \momentVar, \stateVar/\epsilon), \quad (\tau, \momentVar) \in \momentSpace, ~ \stateVar \in \stateSpace
$$
Above, note that the $\stateVar/\epsilon$ in the last coordinate is because $\Prb^\epsilon_\stateVar$ is the distribution associated with $\Xe$, not $\Xee$.
The following result shows us that our parameterization in [](eq:characteristic-asymptotics) and [](eq:LK-asymptotics) applies these cumulant generating functions, where $\aff \defeq \aff^1$ and $\momentSpace \defeq \momentSpace^1$.

<Statement {...affAsymptotics} />
<Statement {...affAsymptoticsRemark} />

<!-- show parameterization for \aff fdds -->
This parameterization also applies to the liftings $\aff^\epsilon(\underline t, \cdot, \cdot)$ of $\aff^\epsilon$ to finite-dimensional projections on partitions $\underline t \vdash [0,\infty)$.
$$
  \Exp_{\Prb^\epsilon_\stateVar}\exp\prj{\underline\momentVar}{\Xe_{\underline t}} \eqdef \exp\aff(\underline t, \underline\momentVar, \stateVar/\epsilon), \quad \underline\momentVar \in \vecSpace^{|\underline t|}, ~ \stateVar\in \stateSpace
$$
Denoting $\aff(\underline t, \cdot, \cdot) \defeq \aff^1(\underline t, \cdot, \cdot)$, the below result shows just this.

<Statement {...affFddAsymptotics} />

<!-- show how this is a mean field regime -->
Now that we have established parameterizations for just about every object that relates to an affine process, we establish some intuition on the relationship between these distributions $(\Prb^\epsilon_\stateVar)_{\epsilon>0}$.
The first of which is immediate from our preceding result, but it only makes sense when we consider the countable sequence $\epsilon_m \defeq 1/m$ for $m \in \bbN$.

<Statement {...meanFieldAsymptotics} />

<!-- show parameterization for Brownian motion and Poisson random measure -->
We may also intuitively understand the relationship of $(\Prb^\epsilon_\stateVar)_{\stateVar\in\stateSpace}$ from a dynamical system perspective.
In [%full](statement:jump-diffusion-characterizations), we see how jump-diffusions $\X$ always correspond to a weak solution of some stochastic differential equation driven by standard Brownian motion $\W$ and Poisson random measure $\poisRM$.
$$
  @tag(sde-reminder)
  \begin{gathered}
    \X_t = \X_0 + \affDrift^\trunc(\X) \shortInt \leb_t + \affDiffSqrt(\X) \shortInt \W_t + \trunc \circ \thinner(\X, \id_\vecSpace) \ast \compensate{\poisRM}_t  + \trunc' \circ \thinner(\X, \id_\vecSpace) \ast \poisRM_t \\
    \forall ~ \stateVar \in \stateSpace, \quad \left\{\begin{aligned}
      \affJump(\stateVar, \Gamma) &= \int_\vecSpace 1_\Gamma\big(\thinner(\stateVar, \markVar)\big) \rmd\markVar, & \Gamma \in \scrB(\vecSpace-\{0\}) \\
      \affDiff(\stateVar) &= \affDiffSqrt\affDiffSqrt^*(\stateVar)
    \end{aligned}\right.
  \end{gathered}
$$
The following proposition gives perspectives on how the processes $\Xe$ may relate through these objects in two different perturbed dynamical systems.

<Statement {...sdeAsymptotics} />
